      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The incidence of dissection following rotational atherectomy was 12.8%. By multivariate analysis tortuosity, primary and non-type B lesions were correlated with an increased incidence of dissection. The procedural success rate was reduced in the presence of dissection (86% vs 96%; p = 0.0001) primarily because patients with dissection required coronary bypass more frequently than those without dissection."},
